{"\ufeffEmployee Leave Management (ELM)\nWorkflow Specifications \u2014 Final Synchronized v1.6\nCorrected Basis-Workflow completeness \u2022 17 complete Basis Workflows \u2022 4 Composite Workflows \u2022 authoritative STTs\n1. Revision Scope and Authority\nVersion 1.6 corrects a Basis-Workflow derivation defect in v1.5: reusable substitute-consent/recovery prefixes were incorrectly counted as Basis Workflows, leaving some complete valid UC sequences (for example EL-UC-001 \u2192 EL-UC-002 \u2192 EL-UC-003 for substitute-required CL/RH) without a corresponding Basis Workflow. No PS, CFR/AFR, UC, or BR semantics are changed.\nThe Composite Workflows remain semantically unchanged. Their constituent Basis-Workflow references are updated to the corrected complete-path set. The State-Transition Table (STT) remains authoritative and each diagram is a corresponding visual view.\n2. Workflow Derivation Decisions\n    1. Derive workflows only from validated state-changing UCs and applicable BRs.\n    2. A Basis Workflow shall be a complete finite valid progression from a meaningful process start/context to a meaningful business outcome": null, " a reusable prefix, suffix, or recovery fragment is not by itself a Basis Workflow unless it independently constitutes such a progression.\n    3. A sequence such as Apply \u2192 Substitute Response \u2192 Unit Head Review must therefore appear as a complete Basis Workflow when it is a valid business path.\n    4. When terminal outcomes differ only in the outcome of the same final decision UC and all preceding steps are identical, they may be represented as alternative terminal rows in one Basis Workflow to avoid duplicate path specifications.\n    5. A purely configuration-controlled optional/bypass step (for example the Establishment routing step) may remain within the same Basis Workflow when it does not create a different business outcome.\n    6. For a meaningful loop, represent zero traversal and exactly one traversal": null, " do not enumerate further equivalent repetitions.\n    7. Composite Workflows integrate complete Basis Workflows and may additionally represent cross-cutting transitions such as pending withdrawal and routing-changing SLA escalation.\n    8. ELM is not its own UC actor. System may appear in an STT only as the performer of a meaningful automatic transition": null, " time/external events remain triggers/guards.\n    9. Pending requests are not modified in place. Change before final approval is handled through withdrawal and, if needed, a fresh application.\n    10. Year-end processing and reminder/notification-only SLA handling remain event-triggered UC+BR behavior, not standalone workflows.\n    11. The STT is authoritative": null, " diagrams must correspond to it exactly.\n3. Workflow Registry\nWorkflow ID\nWorkflow Name\nType\nPurpose / Scope\nConstituent / Related Workflows\nPrimary Related UCs\nBW-EL-01\nNew CL/RH \u2014 No Substitute Gate\nBasis\nCL/RH: no substitute \u2192 Unit Head decision\nCW-EL-01\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-003\nBW-EL-02\nNew CL/RH \u2014 Substitute Accepted (No Loop)\nBasis\nCL/RH: substitute accept \u2192 Unit Head decision\nCW-EL-01\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-002, EL-UC-003\nBW-EL-03\nNew CL/RH \u2014 Substitute Declined, Replacement Accepted (One Loop Traversal)\nBasis\nCL/RH: one decline/replacement loop \u2192 Unit Head decision\nCW-EL-01\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-002, EL-UC-019, EL-UC-003\nBW-EL-04\nNew Higher-Sanction Leave \u2014 No Substitute Gate\nBasis\nHigher-sanction: no substitute \u2192 final decision\nCW-EL-01\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-003, EL-UC-004, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-05\nNew Higher-Sanction Leave \u2014 Substitute Accepted (No Loop)\nBasis\nHigher-sanction: substitute accept \u2192 final decision\nCW-EL-01\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-002, EL-UC-003, EL-UC-004, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-06\nNew Higher-Sanction Leave \u2014 Substitute Declined, Replacement Accepted (One Loop Traversal)\nBasis\nHigher-sanction: one decline/replacement loop \u2192 final decision\nCW-EL-01\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-002, EL-UC-019, EL-UC-003, EL-UC-004, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-07\nDirector Self-Sanction \u2014 No Substitute Gate\nBasis\nDirector: no substitute \u2192 self-sanction decision\nCW-EL-01\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-08\nDirector Self-Sanction \u2014 Substitute Accepted (No Loop)\nBasis\nDirector: substitute accept \u2192 self-sanction decision\nCW-EL-01\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-002, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-09\nDirector Self-Sanction \u2014 Substitute Declined, Replacement Accepted (One Loop Traversal)\nBasis\nDirector: one decline/replacement loop \u2192 self-sanction decision\nCW-EL-01\nEL-UC-001, EL-UC-002, EL-UC-019, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-10\nCL/RH Approved-Leave Cancellation\nBasis\nCL/RH cancellation \u2192 Unit Head decision\nCW-EL-02\nEL-UC-008, EL-UC-003\nBW-EL-11\nHigher-Sanction Approved-Leave Cancellation\nBasis\nHigher-sanction cancellation \u2192 final decision\nCW-EL-02\nEL-UC-008, EL-UC-003, EL-UC-004, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-12\nOngoing Leave Extension \u2014 No Substitute Gate\nBasis\nExtension: no substitute \u2192 final decision\nCW-EL-03\nEL-UC-009, EL-UC-003, EL-UC-004, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-13\nOngoing Leave Extension \u2014 Substitute Accepted (No Loop)\nBasis\nExtension: substitute accept \u2192 final decision\nCW-EL-03\nEL-UC-009, EL-UC-002, EL-UC-003, EL-UC-004, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-14\nOngoing Leave Extension \u2014 Substitute Declined, Replacement Accepted (One Loop Traversal)\nBasis\nExtension: one decline/replacement loop \u2192 final decision\nCW-EL-03\nEL-UC-009, EL-UC-002, EL-UC-019, EL-UC-003, EL-UC-004, EL-UC-005\nBW-EL-15\nNormal Resumption Review\nBasis\nNormal resumption \u2192 review\nCW-EL-04\nEL-UC-010, EL-UC-011\nBW-EL-16\nEarly Resumption Review\nBasis\nEarly resumption \u2192 review and synchronize\nCW-EL-04\nEL-UC-010, EL-UC-011\nBW-EL-17\nLate Resumption Review\nBasis\nLate resumption \u2192 review and synchronize\nCW-EL-04\nEL-UC-010, EL-UC-011\nCW-EL-01\nNew Leave Processing and Pending Withdrawal\nComposite\nIntegrated new-leave progression + pend